Third-party licenses
====================

Part A lists the third-party code compiled into the julia1-cli binaries, with the license texts (1)-(5). Part B lists
the licenses of the model and tokenizer that the converter reads and the documentation refers to (6)-(7); they are not
part of the binaries or of this repository.

A. Code in the julia1-cli binaries
----------------------------------

The julia1-cli binaries (bin/julia1-cli, lib/libjulia1_gguf_native.*, and the same library inside the julia1-gguf
Python wheel) are built from this repository's src/ (Apache License 2.0, see LICENSE) and statically link the code
below, all of it taken from the llama.cpp release v0.5.0 (https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp, tag v0.5.0, archive
SHA-256 fef9ed754f4e031fb5c663c29260feda4ebc241abb68d64a81c0f1df5f1748e2). The license texts follow the list. The ggml
they link carries this repository's patches/ggml-julia1.patch, which is under the MIT License like ggml itself (1).

  component                      source in llama.cpp v0.5.0              in                          license
  ggml 0.25.1 (CPU, BLAS and     ggml/                                    julia1-cli, library         MIT (1)
    Metal backends; the Metal
    shader library is embedded),
    with patches/ggml-julia1.patch
  llamafile sgemm (tinyBLAS)     ggml/src/ggml-cpu/llamafile/sgemm.cpp    julia1-cli, library         MIT (2)
  YaRN RoPE scaling              ggml/src/ggml-cpu/ops.cpp,               julia1-cli, library         MIT (3)
                                 ggml/src/ggml-metal/kernels/rope.metal
                                 (copied into kernels/mul_mm.metal by
