  nlohmann/json 3.12.0           vendor/nlohmann/json.hpp                 julia1-cli, library         MIT (4)
  cpp-httplib 0.57.1             vendor/cpp-httplib/                      julia1-cli only             MIT (5)

Notices carried inside those sources:
  * vendor/nlohmann/json.hpp names, besides Niels Lohmann: Bjoern Hoehrmann (2008-2009, UTF-8 decoder), Florian
    Loitsch (2009, Grisu2 number formatting), Evan Nemerson (2016-2021, Hedley macros) and The Abseil Authors
    (2018, integer_sequence utilities), each under SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT in json.hpp; the Abseil part is
    marked there as taken from Google Abseil (https://github.com/abseil/abseil-cpp), which is licensed under the
    Apache License 2.0 (text in LICENSE).
  * ggml/src/ggml-cpu/vec.h marks its vectorised expf routines (ggml_v_expf) as "adapted from arm limited
    optimized routine" (Arm Optimized Routines, https://github.com/ARM-software/optimized-routines, MIT OR
    Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception), and one SVE routine (compiled only for SVE targets, not for Apple silicon)
    as borrowed from OpenVINO (https://github.com/openvinotoolkit/openvino, Apache License 2.0, text in LICENSE).

The binaries also use system libraries that are not redistributed here: on macOS libSystem, libc++, libobjc and the
Accelerate, Foundation, CoreFoundation, Metal and MetalKit frameworks; on Linux the C/C++ runtime and, when ggml
finds it, the OpenMP runtime (libgomp).

The Julia-1 model weights are not part of these binaries (see NOTICE and part B).

